<component name="ProjectRunConfigurationManager">
  <!--
    App (local debug)

    The default way to run the app, and the only manual step in a debugging
    session: pick it in the toolbar dropdown and press Debug. Nothing here
    needs editing.

    What happens before the app launches
    ===================================
    The `devUp` Gradle task runs first, as a before launch step. It brings the
    whole environment up so that pressing Debug on a cold machine is enough:

      1. builds and starts the pi-server container, detached
      2. waits for GET /health to answer, so the app is never installed
         against a server that is still starting - which presents as a broken
         app rather than a slow one
      3. starts an emulator if no device is attached, and waits for it to
         finish booting

    It is idempotent, so on a second run it costs a couple of seconds and
    confirms the server is still healthy. The implementation is
    scripts/dev-up.sh and scripts/dev-up.ps1 at the repository root; both are
    runnable on their own when something needs investigating.

    It runs before the APK is assembled on purpose. The emulator boot is the
    long pole, so starting it first overlaps with everything else, and if the
    build then fails you still have a warm environment for the retry.

    If you are debugging on a physical tablet over USB, set KG_SKIP_EMULATOR=1
    in the environment and the device step is skipped.

    Where it points
    ===============
    The debug variant builds its URL from `kidsGalaxyDebugServerHost`, which
    is committed in android/local.properties as 10.0.2.2 - the emulator's
    alias for this machine's loopback. That is also where devUp starts the
    server, so the two match with nothing to configure.

    Release uses a separate property, `kidsGalaxyServerHost`, so a value set
    for local debugging cannot follow a field build.

    On a physical tablet, 10.0.2.2 is meaningless - the tablet is a separate
    device. Swap in your machine's LAN address in local.properties:

        kidsGalaxyDebugServerHost=192.168.1.50

    Debug builds talk plain HTTP and attach an OkHttp logging interceptor at
    BASIC level. Watch Logcat filtered to KidsGalaxyApi or KidsGalaxyRepo.

    Running production instead
    =========================
    There is deliberately no run configuration for release. A field build is
    certificate authenticated and must not pick up a developer's local host or
    the placeholder certificate password, both of which would happen silently
    if release were wired into a one click Run button.

    Build it explicitly, from a terminal, stating both values:

        cd pi-server/certs
        SERVER_IP=10.42.0.1 ./generate_certs.sh
        cp client.p12 ca.crt ../../android/app/src/main/assets/
        cd ../../android
        ./gradlew assembleRelease -PkidsGalaxyServerHost=10.42.0.1 -PkidsGalaxyCertPassword=INSTALL_TIME_PASSWORD

    That produces app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk, pinned to the
    project CA and presenting client.p12 on every request. Release builds
    attach no logging interceptor, by design.

    If Studio says "Module is not specified"
    =======================================
    Pick KidsGalaxy.app.main from the Module dropdown and save. The module
    name Studio generates varies slightly between versions, so this one line
    is the only part of this file that may need a local correction.
  -->
  <configuration default="false" name="App (local debug)" type="AndroidRunConfigurationType" factoryName="Android App">
    <module name="KidsGalaxy.app.main" />
    <option name="DEPLOY" value="true" />
    <option name="DEPLOY_APK_FROM_BUNDLE" value="false" />
    <option name="DEPLOY_AS_INSTANT" value="false" />
    <option name="ARTIFACT_NAME" value="" />
    <option name="PM_INSTALL_OPTIONS" value="" />
    <option name="ALL_USERS" value="false" />
    <option name="ALWAYS_INSTALL_WITH_PM" value="false" />
    <option name="CLEAR_APP_STORAGE" value="false" />
    <option name="DYNAMIC_FEATURES_DISABLED_LIST" value="" />
    <option name="ACTIVITY_EXTRA_FLAGS" value="" />
    <option name="MODE" value="default_activity" />
    <method v="2">
      <option name="Gradle.BeforeRunTask" enabled="true" tasks="devUp" externalProjectPath="$PROJECT_DIR$" vmOptions="" scriptParameters="" />
      <option name="Android.Gradle.BeforeRunTask" enabled="true" />
    </method>
  </configuration>
</component>
